  "fixes": [
    "Public and backend A1/zero-slot admission preserve physical span and real row pitch; no S-fold caller copy.",
    "CPU plain BF16 W widens W to F32 rather than pre-narrowing original F32 A; immutable singleton Graph constants use existing cold artifact preparation.",
    "CUDA original plain sorted fallback preserves every repeated slot; previously it stopped at the first matching expert occurrence.",
    "Metal original map kernel emits every repeated slot with O(T*S+E) metadata; shared array carrier retains actual strides and original owner.",
    "Metal result allocation reserves actual backend span, including MMID private metadata after the logical result.",
    "Vulkan qualified non-dense Grouped input boundary retains original read-only layout/backing. Existing dense input alignment adapters remain, including valid 4-byte-offset bindings.",
    "Vulkan native direct-Y MMID/MVID preserve actual span and pitch; non-vector-aligned rows use the existing unaligned variant. Matrix dispatch covers every repeated ID occurrence. No CONT/Repeat or shader ABI addition."
  ],
  "failures_retained": [
    "Apple original T32 repeated-ID native errors; carrier CONT mismatch and insufficient physical result allocation.",
    "CPU Graph immutable singleton missed cold constant preparation.",
    "CUDA fixture lacked ready owned source/destination permission for queued constant preparation; fixture now uses existing ownership APIs.",
    "CUDA nonlinear fused GLU versus standalone exact equality was an invalid oracle; final independent FP64 check retains existing bounded nonlinear error, exact dot/BF16/ID checks unchanged.",
    "Vulkan checked helper dispatch count assumption, padded-input native pitch/span bug and insufficient matrix dispatch rows for duplicate IDs."
  ],
  "costs_and_limits": [
    "Shared A1 descriptor has T*K physical rows, but CUDA original plain sorted fallback still uses T*S*K scratch and host ID readback/synchronization. No universal O(T*K) workspace claim.",
